@cc [owner:fabiencelier,label:product;mcp] changes-are-suggestions
Tools of the `building_agents_and_skills` MCP server MUST NOT modify an agent or a skill directly.
Every tool that proposes a change records a `pending` agent or skill suggestion with source `conversational` for the
editors to review, marks conflicting pending suggestions `outdated`, and returns the suggestion
`sId` embedded in a directive (`:skill_suggestion[]{sId=... kind=... skillId=...}`) so the conversation UI can render it inline.

@cc [owner:avervaet,label:product;security] create-agent-is-direct-and-scoped
`create_agent` directly creates an `AgentConfiguration`, unlike every other tool in this server. It MUST verify the calling user is an interactive workspace member holding the workspace's `create` `agent` permission before creating anything, and MUST restrict what it creates to what that user could already do unilaterally through the builder: the new agent stays `hidden`, editable only by its creator, and carries no attached actions. Publishing an agent workspace-wide, attaching tools, or adding editors MUST remain separate, explicitly-permissioned actions performed afterward.